Dear Marc,

I think you need to assign a distribution to your missing data. For example:

temperature[i,j] ~ dnorm(mu, tau)

And then have some prior distribution on mu and tau. For example:

mu ~ dnorm(10, 0.001) # here you can use the mean temperature and precision you want
tau <- 1 / sigma * sigma
sigma ~ dgamma(0.001, 0.001) # the same here

Thus, you would be able to estimate mu and tau along with the other parameters.
So in you data list you would have temperature as a vector containing your observed values and NAs.

If you have discrete covariates, or the normal distribution is not a good approximation, you should use any other distribution that suits better.

Best regards,
Heloise

